      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Who writes what\n• API (create): jobs row + first job_outbox row in one transaction. Replay: jobs back to QUEUED + new outbox row.\n• Outbox publisher: claims job_outbox rows (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) → PUBLISHING, then PUBLISHED or FAILED.\n• Worker: jobs → PROCESSING (leased_until = start + 6 min) + job_attempts row; then one fenced transaction:\n   final jobs state + attempt outcome + retry or DLQ outbox row (WHERE status = 'PROCESSING' AND attempt = :attempt).\n• JobExecutor: side_effect_receipts row; the unique effect_key stops a duplicate business effect on redelivery.\n• Lease recovery: same fenced transaction as a worker failure, for jobs still PROCESSING after leased_until.",
      "originalText": "Who writes what\n• API (create): jobs row + first job_outbox row in one transaction. Replay: jobs back to QUEUED + new outbox row.\n• Outbox publisher: claims job_outbox rows (FOR UPDATE SKIP LOCKED) → PUBLISHING, then PUBLISHED or FAILED.\n• Worker: jobs → PROCESSING (leased_until = start + 6 min) + job_attempts row; then one fenced transaction:\n   final jobs state + attempt outcome + retry or DLQ outbox row (WHERE status = 'PROCESSING' AND attempt = :attempt).\n• JobExecutor: side_effect_receipts row; the unique effect_key stops a duplicate business effect on redelivery.\n• Lease recovery: same fenced transaction as a worker failure, for jobs still PROCESSING after leased_until.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": "writers",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    }
  ],
